# flyfunboarding secrets: copy to .env.secrets (gitignored, keep it mode 600) and fill in.
# Plain configuration is in .env (see .env.sample / .env.docker.example).
#
# Who reads this file:
#   - docker compose passes it to the container whole via env_file (docker-compose.yml);
#     deploy is a plain `docker compose up -d --build`, no --env-file flags.
#   - the app outside Docker (pydantic settings) reads server/.env then server/.env.secrets
#     (this file wins on duplicate keys; real environment variables beat both).
# In the owner's setup this file is sops-encrypted in the config repo and installed by
# syncfiles on the host that uses it: don't hand-edit it there.
#
# QUOTING RULE - wrap every value in single quotes:   SECRET='p$a${X}#b c"d'
#   - unquoted or "double-quoted" values: compose expands $VAR / ${VAR} (from .env or the
#     shell) and an unquoted ` #` starts a comment. Single quotes are literal in compose,
#     and the app reads both files with interpolation disabled.
#   - don't use `$$` to escape: compose turns it into `$`, the app keeps `$$`.
#   - no backslashes (compose keeps `\\`, the app turns it into `\`); a single quote
#     inside the value is written `\'`. Simplest: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.

# Database password (must match the user in shared-infra MySQL). Required: the server
# refuses to start if it is empty.
DB_PASSWORD='your_db_password'

# Secret for the QR code hash (secret_hash, always used) and the system Bearer token
# (airline/db setup endpoints). Required: the server refuses to start if it is empty.
SECRET='your-secret-key-here'

# Password of CERTIFICATE_PATH, only used when that is a .p12 file. Prod signs with
# certs/certificate.pem + certs/certificate.key, so it is empty there.
CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD=''
